{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the lot</b> — two times here, and the other (instance): וגורל לבוזזינו (\"and the lot of our plunderers\"). This is Haman, about whom it is written: ויבז בעיניו (\"and he despised in his eyes\"), and he cast lots over Israel. Said HaShem: He is not worth it to you — already I cast lots, and the lot of my portion fell in Israel above all 70 nations. This is what is written: גורל אחד לה' וגורל אחד לעזאזל (\"one lot for YHWH and one lot for Azazel\"), which atones for the sins of Israel, as written: ונשא עונותם (\"and he bears their sins\") — עונות תם (\"their sins\" complete), it atones. Three times in the Masorah: עזאזל — corresponding to נושא עון ופשע וחטאה (\"bearing iniquity and transgression and sin\"), in the merit of the three patriarchs."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase וגורל לבוזזינו appears to be a citation, possibly from a piyyut or midrashic source, rendered here as written. The parenthetical צ\"ל דלא חשיב דמשלח is a textual note indicating the expected reading 'that the one sent [to Azazel] is not counted'; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:39.107418783Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}